<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="CheektoCheek-C-Theme" spTempo="144">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1935
Composer:	Irving Berlin
Lyricist:	Irving Berlin
Form:	72-bar AABCA
Style:	Swing
Key:	C major

“Cheek to Cheek” was written for the 1935 film
Top Hat, where Fred Astaire introduced it while
dancing with Ginger Rogers. Sources variously
date the composition to 1934 and its film release
and commercial publication to 1935; 1935 is used
here as the song’s standard publication and debut
year. Its form is sometimes analyzed as AABA,
but the bridge’s contrasting minor coloring and the
return structure support the more detailed AABCA
description. </spComments>
